From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:44:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] overview: Hold a card halfway away for a second to force
 quit its app

An app that does not close its window when asked to comes back to the
overview a second after it was swiped away, and there was nothing else
to do about it. Swiping its card at least halfway away and holding it
there for a second now gives a short vibration and asks whether to
force quit the app; once released the card goes back instead of
closing. Other swipe-away bins (notifications, dialogs) are unchanged.

Force quitting kills every process of the systemd user units that run
exactly the app's id (app-gnome-<id>-<pid>.scope, app-flatpak-...,
dbus-:1.2-<id>@1.service), never Phosh's own unit, so a terminal is not
hit for an app started from it. Without such a unit the dialog says
that no running process was found. An Android app of Waydroid's
multi-window mode (waydroid.<package>) is stopped by Waydroid's helper
through pkexec (am force-stop). The question goes away when the app
closes after all and when the phone locks.
